# Rust / Cargo
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock is committed for binaries (Aurora ships applications),
# so it is deliberately NOT ignored.

# Build & profiling artifacts
/dist/
*.profraw
*.profdata
perf.data*
flamegraph.svg
criterion/

# Test output
# Golden-image baselines are committed; only failure diffs are ignored.
**/tests/**/*.actual.png
**/tests/**/*.diff.png
/target/nextest/

# Large binary corpora — fetched by script, never committed (PRD §13 Step 6).
# Ignore the fetched fixture trees specifically, not the whole /corpora/ dir,
# so the small fetch scripts/manifests/generated inventories stay tracked —
# same split as /spike/raw-icc/reference/raw-samples/ below.
/corpora/psd/reference/psd-tools-fixtures/
/assets/samples/

# Local development
.env
.env.local
*.local.toml
# Session-scratch project-state summary, regenerated locally and never a
# source of truth (PLAN.md is). Accidentally committed in 0.94.0,
# untracked, then accidentally committed again in 0.95.0 -- hence the
# ignore, added in 0.95.1 so it cannot come back a third time.
/report.md

# Editors & IDEs
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Aurora runtime output
*.aur.bak
/scratch/
aurora.log
crash-reports/

# Spike build output (the spike is outside the workspace, so /target misses it)
/spike/*/target/
/spike/psd-write/out/
/spike/a11y-ime/result-*.md
/spike/raw-icc/out/
# Real camera RAW samples: multi-MB each, PLAN 0.7's "corpora are gitignored"
# rule. Re-fetch with reference/fetch-samples.sh. ICC profiles in the same
# reference/ tree are small (CC0) and are committed normally.
/spike/raw-icc/reference/raw-samples/
